======================================================================================================================
ITEM 120 -- the Upsilon the cosmological constant predicts, against DiskMass, localised
======================================================================================================================

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART 1 -- the overlap between SPARC and DiskMass
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DiskMass PPak sample (the DMS VII galaxies): 31 UGC numbers; DiskMass parent sample: 231; SPARC carries 76 UGC galaxies out of 175
  overlap by UGC number: PPak n SPARC = EMPTY; parent n SPARC = ['UGC07690']
  independent sky-position cross-match of the 31 PPak galaxies against SPARC: nearest SPARC galaxy is 13.2 arcmin away at best, 5.2 degrees typically -- so the empty overlap is real and not a name-matching failure
  inclination, the variable that makes them disjoint: DiskMass 19-45 deg (median 31), SPARC's analysis sample 30-90 deg (median 62); SPARC's master table reaches 15 deg but those galaxies are cut, so the usable floor is 30 deg and 39% of the DiskMass sample lies below it
  [PASS] 120a THE ITEM AS POSED HAS AN EMPTY DOMAIN, and the reason is structural.  SPARC and the DiskMass PPak sample share no galaxies at all -- checked by UGC number and independently by sky position -- because DiskMass selects discs nearly face-on so that its vertical dispersion is measurable and SPARC selects discs inclined enough to deproject a rotation speed.  'Item 76 restricted to the DiskMass overlap' therefore cannot be computed, now or ever, and the rest of this script localises the disagreement without one   (PPak n SPARC = 0 galaxies; parent n SPARC = 1 (['UGC07690']), and that one is not in the PPak subsample; nearest position match 13.2 arcmin)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART 2 -- the framework's required Upsilon, per galaxy, on the DiskMass galaxies
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  22 DMS VII galaxies carry a kinematic inclination, a disc scale length, a distance, a rotation amplitude and a K magnitude -- the same 22 item 17 used
  CAVEAT INHERITED FROM ITEM 17 AND NOT WEAKENED HERE: DMS XI's V_rot is a PROJECTED amplitude and is deprojected by
  1/sin(i) with the kinematic inclination.  Item 17 chose that convention among three by checking which put the
  sample on SPARC's baryonic Tully-Fisher zero-point.  The convention itself is the standard, physically correct one
  and uses measured inclinations, so the per-galaxy numbers below are determined by measured quantities -- but the
  AGREEMENT of this sample's zero-point with SPARC's is not independent evidence, and is not used as any below.

